WEBVTT

00:00:14.318 --> 00:00:15.536
Shaxs has the gym in 20,

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:17.103
but we should have time
for a quick round.

00:00:17.147 --> 00:00:19.236
Ooh, you guys gonna go 'anbo?
Can I get in on that?

00:00:19.279 --> 00:00:21.151
Sure! More the merrier.

00:00:21.194 --> 00:00:22.543
Three months of midnight
practice

00:00:22.587 --> 00:00:23.936
-is finally gonna pay off.

00:00:23.979 --> 00:00:26.417
Can't wait to see the
look on her face.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.119
Glad you're still into this.
I was worried

00:00:33.163 --> 00:00:34.947
maybe I came down
too hard on you last time.

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:36.862
Hopefully we picked up
a few of your moves.

00:00:36.905 --> 00:00:40.170
Nothing like some friendly
Anbo-jyutsu to work up a sweat.

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:47.133
Ha. We've been training on
the holodeck at night.

00:00:47.177 --> 00:00:49.135
You might want to take off
the kid gloves.

00:00:49.179 --> 00:00:50.571
Oh. Ah...

00:00:50.615 --> 00:00:53.052
-Are you okay? I didn't mean...
-I'm great.

00:00:53.096 --> 00:00:55.359
I can finally
get in a real workout.

00:00:55.402 --> 00:00:57.361
Uh...

00:01:02.235 --> 00:01:03.758
Oh, God.
No, no, no, no!

00:01:08.154 --> 00:01:10.243
Ah! Ah!

00:01:10.287 --> 00:01:13.768
Put the kid gloves on!
Put the kid gloves on!

00:01:13.812 --> 00:01:14.987
Shaxs! Help!

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.902
Don't worry about me,
I'm early.

00:01:16.945 --> 00:01:18.164
You've still got ten minutes.

00:02:32.891 --> 00:02:35.067
Well, if raktajino makes you
all jumpy,

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:37.156
then just switch to
human coffee.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:38.244
Eh, I tried,

00:02:38.288 --> 00:02:39.245
-but it's too weak...

00:02:39.289 --> 00:02:41.378
Shh! Did you hear something?

00:02:43.118 --> 00:02:44.424
Ah. Ah, ah, ah, ah...

00:02:44.468 --> 00:02:45.512
-Ah!

00:02:51.692 --> 00:02:55.696
&lt;i&gt;Captain's log,&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:57.959
&lt;i&gt;the&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos &lt;i&gt;is en route
to Frylon IV&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:58.003 --> 00:03:00.788
&lt;i&gt;to investigate the reported
sighting of a mugato,&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:00.832 --> 00:03:03.748
&lt;i&gt;a dangerous creature not
indigenous to this planet.&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:03.791 --> 00:03:06.664
"Poisonous, carnivorous,
strength of ten men."

00:03:06.707 --> 00:03:08.361
Huh, sounds like my ex.

00:03:08.405 --> 00:03:11.277
I can't believe we pulled
another animal control op,

00:03:11.321 --> 00:03:14.280
as if there weren't more
important jobs for us to do.

00:03:14.324 --> 00:03:17.457
The bio-electrical signatures
on Frylon has made it difficult

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:18.937
to pinpoint life signs,

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:21.374
but with boots on the ground,
we'll find her.

00:03:23.942 --> 00:03:27.293
Let's see, hmm, hmm, hmm...
What about...

00:03:27.337 --> 00:03:29.991
a ten percent gratuity
on a biannual basis?

00:03:30.035 --> 00:03:31.297
Hmm, worth considering...

00:03:31.341 --> 00:03:32.777
-What up?!
Ah!

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:34.387
Wow, flinch much?
Hey, work later.

00:03:34.431 --> 00:03:36.737
Let's hit the phaser range.
I need moving targets.

00:03:36.781 --> 00:03:38.304
This isn't work,
we're playing Diplomath.

00:03:38.348 --> 00:03:40.567
And, we're at a crucial point
in the negotiation.

00:03:40.611 --> 00:03:43.135
-We're both about to lose!
-Why is that good?

00:03:43.178 --> 00:03:44.832
If both sides are equally
unsatisfied

00:03:44.876 --> 00:03:46.965
with the negotiation,
you can close the deal!

00:03:47.008 --> 00:03:48.488
Ready for final offers?

00:03:49.402 --> 00:03:52.840
-Eh, I don't like it.
-I guess I can live with that.

00:03:52.884 --> 00:03:55.321
-That's a compromise!
-Oh, boy.

00:03:55.365 --> 00:03:57.497
I'd say you guys should take up
a less-embarrassing hobby,

00:03:57.541 --> 00:03:58.890
but it might be too late.

00:04:01.371 --> 00:04:03.198
Honus!
Can we get two more?

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:05.200
Yeah, maybe with some
pain reliever mixed in?

00:04:05.244 --> 00:04:08.160
Ah, yeah. Not surprised
you fellas need a drink

00:04:08.203 --> 00:04:10.858
after talkin' with that
powder keg friend of yours.

00:04:10.902 --> 00:04:12.251
Huh? You talking about Mariner?

00:04:12.295 --> 00:04:15.123
If'n that's her real name.

00:04:15.167 --> 00:04:17.648
Haven't you boys ever wondered
how she's able to

00:04:17.691 --> 00:04:21.739
kick so much ass and get away
with whatever she wants?

00:04:21.782 --> 00:04:24.437
Uh, 'cause her mom's the captain
and she practices kicking a lot?

00:04:24.481 --> 00:04:25.612
Usually on us.

00:04:25.656 --> 00:04:27.484
Workin' the bar, I hear a lot

00:04:27.527 --> 00:04:29.268
of inside information.

00:04:29.312 --> 00:04:32.445
Your friend is a specially
trained secret agent

00:04:32.489 --> 00:04:35.579
for Starfleet black ops.

00:04:35.622 --> 00:04:37.842
-Ha-ha-ha. Shut up, Honus!
-Yeah, right, okay, man.

00:04:37.885 --> 00:04:40.627
I'm telling you, they made her
into a killing machine.

00:04:40.671 --> 00:04:41.846
The perfect weapon.

00:04:41.889 --> 00:04:43.326
We spend all of our time
with Mariner.

00:04:43.369 --> 00:04:46.067
Pretty sure we'd know
if she was "the perfect weapon."

00:04:46.111 --> 00:04:47.417
Most of the time
she's napping.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:49.854
Of course she does.
Captain's daughter,

00:04:49.897 --> 00:04:51.769
friends with the
softest guys on the ship;

00:04:51.812 --> 00:04:53.118
it's the perfect cover.

00:04:53.161 --> 00:04:54.859
Haven't you ever noticed
that she seems to know

00:04:54.902 --> 00:04:56.251
every fightin' style?

00:04:56.295 --> 00:04:57.992
She is a master of
Anbo-jyutsu...

00:04:58.036 --> 00:05:00.386
Look, we may be soft,
but we're not gullible.

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:03.128
Just watch out. When her back's
against the wall,

00:05:03.171 --> 00:05:05.173
that's when
the training kicks in.

00:05:05.217 --> 00:05:09.177
She's programmed to protect
herself at all costs.

00:05:10.788 --> 00:05:14.139
All costs.

00:05:14.182 --> 00:05:16.359
Okay, buddy, you heard wrong.

00:05:16.402 --> 00:05:19.449
I bet they didn't believe the
rumors on the &lt;i&gt;Atlantis&lt;/i&gt; either,

00:05:19.492 --> 00:05:21.451
until it was too late,
and they were all...

00:05:21.494 --> 00:05:23.104
Honus, could you get
back to work?!

00:05:23.148 --> 00:05:25.150
Billups is still waiting
on his peach daiquiri.

00:05:25.193 --> 00:05:28.066
Ah, keep your pips on, Billups.

00:05:28.109 --> 00:05:29.676
-That guy's so full of it.
-Yeah, right?

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:31.983
As if Starfleet would ever hide
a black ops agent

00:05:32.026 --> 00:05:33.419
-on one of their own ships.
-Yeah.

00:05:33.463 --> 00:05:35.334
I mean, Starfleet Intelligence
does it.

00:05:35.378 --> 00:05:37.336
And Tuvok did it when
he infiltrated the Maquis.

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:39.207
And there were a ton during
the Dominion War.

00:05:39.251 --> 00:05:41.601
But on the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos?
Yeah, right.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:42.863 --> 00:05:45.300
Yeah, right...

00:05:48.216 --> 00:05:50.480
Oh! Looks like we have
a spike in the subcortical.

00:05:50.523 --> 00:05:51.785
Let's move, people!

00:05:51.829 --> 00:05:54.048
I need 30cc's of
desalinated paviatic fluid.

00:05:54.092 --> 00:05:55.920
-On it.
-Uh, technically,

00:05:55.963 --> 00:05:57.182
that's my patient.

00:05:57.225 --> 00:05:58.226
Clear the area!

00:05:58.270 --> 00:05:59.619
That's fine. I...

00:05:59.663 --> 00:06:02.361
Ensign Tendi, my office.

00:06:02.405 --> 00:06:04.624
I'm sorry, Doctor, I know you
said I need to be

00:06:04.668 --> 00:06:06.321
-more assertive, I just...
-Okay, okay, whatever.

00:06:06.365 --> 00:06:09.107
This is a list of crew who've
avoided their annual physicals.

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:11.762
But why? The biometric scan
is non-invasive.

00:06:11.805 --> 00:06:14.373
Some freaks hate being
reduced to a set of readings.

00:06:14.417 --> 00:06:16.636
I need you to hunt them down
and scan their asses.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:17.985
You got what it takes?

00:06:18.029 --> 00:06:19.857
Yes! Thank you for this
opportunity.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:21.467
I won't let you down.

00:06:21.511 --> 00:06:23.600
So I was reading up
on the mugatos.

00:06:23.643 --> 00:06:25.993
Did you know they have
alternative pronunciations?

00:06:26.037 --> 00:06:28.343
Mogatu, mugutu, and gumato.

00:06:28.387 --> 00:06:29.954
Isn't that neat
and inconsistent?

00:06:29.997 --> 00:06:31.390
-Mm.
-Dude, I'm talking

00:06:31.434 --> 00:06:32.478
alien pronunciations here.

00:06:32.522 --> 00:06:33.479
That's, like,
your favorite thing.

00:06:33.523 --> 00:06:34.524
-What's up?
-Check this out.

00:06:34.567 --> 00:06:36.395
Mariner's record.

00:06:36.439 --> 00:06:38.441
Don't tell me you actually
believe that bartender.

00:06:38.484 --> 00:06:40.486
Mariner has served
on a lot of ships.

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:42.270
Because she's always
getting demoted.

00:06:42.314 --> 00:06:43.663
Yeah. That's what &lt;i&gt;she&lt;/i&gt; says.

00:06:43.707 --> 00:06:45.491
Look. When she served
on the &lt;i&gt;Atlantis,&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:45.535 --> 00:06:47.406
half the crew
mysteriously vanished.

00:06:47.450 --> 00:06:49.060
I'm sure it was just
a reassignment.

00:06:49.103 --> 00:06:50.453
A hundred reassignments?
Plus,

00:06:50.496 --> 00:06:52.193
there's nothing
in the logs about it.

00:06:52.237 --> 00:06:54.500
Just one day, poof, all gone.

00:06:54.544 --> 00:06:57.024
That is weird. You don't think
she had anything to do with it?

00:06:57.068 --> 00:06:59.766
-Who to do with what?

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:02.160
-Whoa! You guys see that?

00:07:02.203 --> 00:07:04.989
-What's got you so jumpy?

00:07:05.032 --> 00:07:06.686
Just excited to see a mugato.

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:10.560
Oh, you would be. Just stay out
of my way down there. Or else.

00:07:10.603 --> 00:07:11.952
Aah! Or else what?

00:07:11.996 --> 00:07:13.998
I don't know, we'll get poisoned
by a mugato.

00:07:14.041 --> 00:07:16.087
You guys are so weird sometimes.

00:07:20.395 --> 00:07:23.877
Shaxs, our sensors indicate
a storm moving in.

00:07:23.921 --> 00:07:25.662
You've got less than 22 minutes

00:07:25.705 --> 00:07:27.011
&lt;i&gt;before we lose comms.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:27.054 --> 00:07:29.143
Copy that, Captain.
You all got the briefing.

00:07:29.187 --> 00:07:31.798
No weapons.
These mugutus are endangered,

00:07:31.842 --> 00:07:34.497
and their genitals
are sensitive to phaser fire.

00:07:43.854 --> 00:07:45.159
All right, fan out.

00:07:45.203 --> 00:07:47.597
This is where we detected
a gumato life sign.

00:07:49.076 --> 00:07:51.688
Ah, what have we here?

00:07:51.731 --> 00:07:54.255
-Mugato dung.
-Ew!

00:07:54.299 --> 00:07:56.780
-Fresh. Tangy.

00:07:58.651 --> 00:08:00.435
She doesn't seem dangerous.

00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:01.915
I think we're being
silly billies.

00:08:01.959 --> 00:08:04.265
Even if Mariner was black ops,
which she is not,

00:08:04.309 --> 00:08:05.571
that bartender said
she'd only flip out

00:08:05.615 --> 00:08:07.181
if her back was against
the wall.

00:08:07.225 --> 00:08:08.966
This is just one random
mugato, we're fine.

00:08:14.667 --> 00:08:17.801
Yo, it's pretty clear we're
going in the right direction.

00:08:17.844 --> 00:08:19.803
You don't have to...

00:08:19.846 --> 00:08:21.195
Mm-hmm.

00:08:23.633 --> 00:08:25.460
Oh.

00:08:28.768 --> 00:08:30.248
Ferengi.

00:08:37.864 --> 00:08:39.300
Clear them out, fools.

00:08:39.344 --> 00:08:41.389
I need to show off
the fresh merchandise.

00:08:41.433 --> 00:08:44.697
I'll take a dozen horns.
Are they horns or tusks?

00:08:44.741 --> 00:08:46.351
They're whatever
you want them to be,

00:08:46.394 --> 00:08:49.441
as long as your latinum's
gold-pressed.

00:08:49.484 --> 00:08:51.486
They're harvesting
these animals.

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:53.010
Boimler to &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:53.053 --> 00:08:54.359
Look, they've got a signal
dampener.

00:08:54.402 --> 00:08:55.882
It's jamming this whole area.

00:08:55.926 --> 00:08:57.362
Looks like we're on our own.

00:08:57.405 --> 00:08:59.930
Just how I like it,
backs against the wall.

00:08:59.973 --> 00:09:01.453
I think we should
retreat and...

00:09:01.496 --> 00:09:03.281
-Let's move.

00:09:04.978 --> 00:09:07.111
Starfleet!

00:09:07.154 --> 00:09:09.679
Ferengi poachers,
you are violating

00:09:09.722 --> 00:09:12.507
the conservation laws
of Federation space.

00:09:12.551 --> 00:09:15.467
Oh, this is Federation space?

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:17.077
I didn't know that.
Did you know that?

00:09:17.121 --> 00:09:20.559
Oh, thank the maker you're here.
I was being attacked by these...

00:09:20.603 --> 00:09:22.474
You were purchasing
illegal horns.

00:09:22.517 --> 00:09:24.389
Stand down and prepare
to be searched.

00:09:24.432 --> 00:09:28.219
Hey, no need for all this.
We're licensed businessmen.

00:09:28.262 --> 00:09:30.874
Oh, really?
You have a permit?

00:09:30.917 --> 00:09:33.572
Yes, a permit to whip you!

00:09:41.319 --> 00:09:43.408
Mugato stampede!
-Take cover!

00:09:52.939 --> 00:09:55.725
-What do we do?!
-I don't know! Where's Shaxs?!

00:09:55.768 --> 00:09:59.642
No! Aah...

00:09:59.685 --> 00:10:02.166
It's real.
She's going to kill us!

00:10:03.776 --> 00:10:05.822
But there's mugatos out there!

00:10:05.865 --> 00:10:07.519
Yeah, but she's in here!

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:17.747
&lt;i&gt;Captain,
we have an unknown ship&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:17.790 --> 00:10:18.922
&lt;i&gt;leaving the planet's orbit.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:18.965 --> 00:10:21.272
-One occupant.
-Hail them.

00:10:21.315 --> 00:10:23.622
&lt;i&gt;Leave me alone.
I don't have any horns.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:23.666 --> 00:10:26.712
What? I just want to know if
you encountered our away team.

00:10:26.756 --> 00:10:29.062
Not interested.
Don't hail me again.

00:10:29.628 --> 00:10:31.543
Wha-- Put a tractor beam
on that ship.

00:10:31.586 --> 00:10:33.980
I think we need to have
a little chat.

00:10:36.766 --> 00:10:39.159
Captain, his ship--
the hull's integrity's failing.

00:10:39.203 --> 00:10:41.684
What the--
Emergency transport, now!

00:10:43.076 --> 00:10:45.557
What in the name of...

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:46.950
My ship!

00:10:46.993 --> 00:10:48.691
I said the tractor beam!

00:10:48.734 --> 00:10:51.563
It was, Captain!
At the lowest tractor factor.

00:10:51.606 --> 00:10:55.001
My whole life was on that ship.
What have you done?

00:10:57.612 --> 00:10:59.571
We need to get out of range of
their signal dampeners,

00:10:59.614 --> 00:11:02.008
put some distance between us and
Mariner, and contact the ship.

00:11:02.052 --> 00:11:03.444
Was she eating Shaxs?

00:11:03.488 --> 00:11:04.663
That's freakin' crazy, man,
that's just...

00:11:07.448 --> 00:11:09.668
-Go!

00:11:22.507 --> 00:11:25.336
Easy, mates.
You're safe with me.

00:11:25.379 --> 00:11:27.207
Great. Uh, who are you?

00:11:27.251 --> 00:11:28.687
I'm Patingi.

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:31.821
The renowned biologist?

00:11:31.864 --> 00:11:35.476
I have five books on mugatos.

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:37.304
For real? Can you
help us get out of here?

00:11:37.348 --> 00:11:38.871
Of course, mates.

00:11:38.915 --> 00:11:41.700
I've been studying these
beautiful mooga-toes for years.

00:11:41.744 --> 00:11:43.006
I'll walk you right to safety.

00:11:43.049 --> 00:11:45.748
-Oh, you're the best, Patingi!
-I know.

00:11:45.791 --> 00:11:48.968
Come on. Stay low. Follow me.

00:11:50.622 --> 00:11:53.059
-Man, Patingi rules.
-Right?

00:11:54.844 --> 00:11:57.411
H-Hi, Lieutenant!
Sorry to bother you,

00:11:57.455 --> 00:11:58.891
but it says here that you
haven't come in

00:11:58.935 --> 00:12:01.111
-for your annual physical?
-Uh, I'm pretty busy.

00:12:01.154 --> 00:12:02.634
I'll get to it when I get to it.

00:12:02.677 --> 00:12:04.288
Well, actually,
time is of the essence, and...

00:12:04.331 --> 00:12:07.291
I said I'm busy.

00:12:10.381 --> 00:12:11.599
Patingi, are we gonna be
in your next book?

00:12:11.643 --> 00:12:13.776
Hmm? Oh, no,
I don't write, mate.

00:12:13.819 --> 00:12:15.952
I've &lt;i&gt;read&lt;/i&gt; five books
on moo-goes.

00:12:15.995 --> 00:12:18.519
-Wait. What?
-Yeah, I figured I knew enough

00:12:18.563 --> 00:12:20.217
to walk amongst them.

00:12:22.349 --> 00:12:25.091
-See? I'm like one of their own.

00:12:26.658 --> 00:12:28.181
Aah! Patingi!

00:12:28.225 --> 00:12:31.315
-♪

00:12:35.362 --> 00:12:37.669
I'm really committed to fitness.

00:12:37.712 --> 00:12:39.714
I spot Ransom, like,
all the time.

00:12:39.758 --> 00:12:40.846
We're really good pals.

00:12:40.890 --> 00:12:42.674
Lemme get another...

00:12:42.717 --> 00:12:44.981
Thank you for the DNA scan,
Lieutenant.

00:12:45.024 --> 00:12:47.113
Ooh, it says here you
should be drinking more milk

00:12:47.157 --> 00:12:49.202
-because your bones are so weak.

00:12:49.246 --> 00:12:51.596
Hey, don't listen to her,
I'm as strong as...

00:12:51.639 --> 00:12:53.903
-Oh, God, my hip!

00:12:53.946 --> 00:12:57.297
Stevens to T'Ana.
Emergency transport.

00:13:04.087 --> 00:13:05.610
If we ever get off
this planet,

00:13:05.653 --> 00:13:07.090
we'll have to
turn in Mariner, won't we?

00:13:07.133 --> 00:13:09.135
Yeah. Feels bad,
reporting anyone in Starfleet,

00:13:09.179 --> 00:13:10.658
much less a friend.

00:13:10.702 --> 00:13:12.182
Was she our friend?
Or were we just cover for...

00:13:12.225 --> 00:13:13.836
-Shh!

00:13:16.708 --> 00:13:19.580
Quick. In there.

00:13:24.847 --> 00:13:27.197
-Aah!

00:13:29.025 --> 00:13:30.243
What are they doing?

00:13:30.287 --> 00:13:32.942
Oh, God, they're mating.

00:13:39.252 --> 00:13:40.645
-Ah...

00:13:40.688 --> 00:13:43.256
-We're gonna drown.
-Come on, come on.

00:13:45.519 --> 00:13:47.565
Crap! Another one!

00:13:51.264 --> 00:13:53.223
Oh, this could get
violent if he tries

00:13:53.266 --> 00:13:54.702
to assert dominance.

00:14:01.361 --> 00:14:02.406
Is he asserting?

00:14:02.449 --> 00:14:05.365
No. I-I think he likes to watch.

00:14:07.672 --> 00:14:10.414
All right, who's next?

00:14:29.999 --> 00:14:32.175
Huh.

00:14:32.218 --> 00:14:35.178
Who are you?

00:14:35.221 --> 00:14:37.658
Okay, they wore themselves out.

00:14:37.702 --> 00:14:40.009
Ew, gross.
Even the watcher.

00:14:40.052 --> 00:14:42.359
Do you think the captain knows
Mariner's undercover?

00:14:42.402 --> 00:14:43.708
Probably her idea.

00:14:43.751 --> 00:14:45.144
Oh, man, so the
mom-and-daughter thing

00:14:45.188 --> 00:14:46.319
was all an act.

00:14:46.363 --> 00:14:47.407
We were so stupid

00:14:47.451 --> 00:14:48.626
-not to see it.
-Wait.

00:14:49.366 --> 00:14:52.499
Watch it. Mugato trap.

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:55.633
-Hi!
-Aah! Run!

00:14:55.676 --> 00:14:56.982
What the hell are
you two doing?!

00:14:59.028 --> 00:15:00.551
Guys, quick!
The Ferengi are coming.

00:15:00.594 --> 00:15:01.900
You've gotta get me out
of here so...

00:15:01.944 --> 00:15:03.554
So you can eat us,
just like Shaxs?!

00:15:03.597 --> 00:15:05.512
-What?!
-We saw it, Mariner.

00:15:05.556 --> 00:15:06.557
Back there at the compound.

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:08.733
Shaxs was stung by a mugato!

00:15:08.776 --> 00:15:10.169
Yeah, and you stabbed him
and licked his blood.

00:15:10.213 --> 00:15:11.997
They really messed you up good
in that lab.

00:15:12.041 --> 00:15:15.174
I had to suck the venom out!
What lab?

00:15:15.218 --> 00:15:16.567
We know what you really are.

00:15:16.610 --> 00:15:18.003
Wait, wait, wait, wait,
did you find out

00:15:18.047 --> 00:15:19.570
that I'm a black ops
secret agent?

00:15:19.613 --> 00:15:22.007
-You aren't even hiding it?!
-Section 31!

00:15:22.051 --> 00:15:23.617
I am not a spy, guys.

00:15:23.661 --> 00:15:25.097
Then how did you know?

00:15:25.141 --> 00:15:26.533
Because I started that rumor.

00:15:26.577 --> 00:15:28.318
Yeah, right,
more black ops lies.

00:15:28.361 --> 00:15:31.321
No, really, that was me.
Look, I like having a mystique.

00:15:31.364 --> 00:15:32.670
Even if we did believe you,

00:15:32.713 --> 00:15:34.019
how do you explain
the &lt;i&gt;Atlantis?&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:34.063 --> 00:15:35.151
Half the crew
disappeared with no explanation.

00:15:35.194 --> 00:15:36.456
Did you eat them?

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:37.718
The &lt;i&gt;Atlantis?&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:37.762 --> 00:15:39.764
No, everyone
got Kerplickian lice.

00:15:39.807 --> 00:15:41.331
Of course Starfleet Command
didn't put it

00:15:41.374 --> 00:15:42.723
in the official records.

00:15:42.767 --> 00:15:44.508
Do you know
how embarrassing it is

00:15:44.551 --> 00:15:46.771
to lose a starship to lice?

00:15:46.814 --> 00:15:48.294
Why are you so good
at martial arts?

00:15:48.338 --> 00:15:50.035
Because it's a sport I can
practice on my own,

00:15:50.079 --> 00:15:52.124
because on every ship,
I never have friends who--

00:15:52.168 --> 00:15:54.866
Wait, you-you looked up
my records?

00:15:54.909 --> 00:15:58.087
You guys, you thought I was
an undercover killer?

00:15:58.130 --> 00:16:00.045
Ow! What the hell?!

00:16:00.089 --> 00:16:01.916
-Oh, I thought you just...
-Because before you did, and

00:16:01.960 --> 00:16:03.396
-it was like you were a ninja.
-...might catch the tricorder...

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:05.746
Yeah, but-- That's all it took
is a lucky catch?

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:07.183
You shouldn't have started
that rumor.

00:16:07.226 --> 00:16:08.793
I mean,
"Kill anything in her way"?

00:16:08.836 --> 00:16:10.142
Why would you want people
to think that?

00:16:10.186 --> 00:16:12.231
Because it keeps jerks
away from me.

00:16:12.275 --> 00:16:14.190
But I can't believe you guys
would ever believe that.

00:16:14.233 --> 00:16:15.756
You're my best friends.

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:18.237
I-I think we believed because
that part made sense.

00:16:18.281 --> 00:16:20.413
That a badass like you wouldn't
really be friends

00:16:20.457 --> 00:16:21.762
with guys like us.

00:16:21.806 --> 00:16:24.287
-Aw, guys, I... Oh, crap.

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:26.419
-It's too late. Hide.
-We're not leaving you!

00:16:26.463 --> 00:16:29.379
The Ferengi got everyone else.
It's up to you guys!

00:16:29.422 --> 00:16:30.771
But what do we do?

00:16:30.815 --> 00:16:32.382
You have to be the black ops
super spies.

00:16:32.425 --> 00:16:34.253
Kick their asses!

00:16:39.258 --> 00:16:42.131
Ah, what a catch. Take her!

00:16:57.015 --> 00:16:58.799
Any luck with those physicals?

00:16:58.843 --> 00:17:00.975
I'm almost done,
just one holdout left.

00:17:01.019 --> 00:17:02.890
Really?
I'm impressed, Ensign.

00:17:02.934 --> 00:17:04.805
This last one, it's weird.

00:17:04.849 --> 00:17:06.242
It's not even a name,

00:17:06.285 --> 00:17:08.113
-it's just a serial number.
-Ah.

00:17:08.157 --> 00:17:10.246
Well, probably just an error
in the system.

00:17:10.289 --> 00:17:13.423
It's almost as if someone erased
their information.

00:17:13.466 --> 00:17:15.468
Yeah, I mean, there's always one
that slips through the cracks.

00:17:15.512 --> 00:17:17.253
We've wasted enough time
on this. Come on.

00:17:17.296 --> 00:17:20.125
Ugh, I just really wanted
to finish this job for you.

00:17:20.169 --> 00:17:22.171
Enough! Go back to
your station, Ensign.

00:17:24.825 --> 00:17:26.958
That number.

00:17:27.001 --> 00:17:28.786
You're the last holdout?

00:17:31.005 --> 00:17:33.443
Congratulations. You got me.

00:17:33.486 --> 00:17:36.228
I-I just don't understand.
Why not just get your exam?

00:17:36.272 --> 00:17:39.144
You want me to see a doctor?
I am the doctor!

00:17:39.188 --> 00:17:40.841
When I picked you for this job,

00:17:40.885 --> 00:17:42.974
I was counting on you
to give up.

00:17:43.017 --> 00:17:44.715
Maybe the old Tendi
was a pushover,

00:17:44.758 --> 00:17:47.935
but a lot's changed
since slightly earlier today.

00:17:49.198 --> 00:17:51.983
All right, let's just
get this over with.

00:17:52.026 --> 00:17:55.595
-Get back here!

00:17:55.639 --> 00:17:58.946
Bad Dr. T'Ana. Bad!

00:18:10.262 --> 00:18:12.308
Mr. Hyde, while we can't
replace your ship,

00:18:12.351 --> 00:18:15.659
I can offer you one of our
shuttlecrafts.

00:18:15.702 --> 00:18:17.226
I think that's more than fair.

00:18:17.269 --> 00:18:18.401
Hmm...

00:18:18.444 --> 00:18:20.490
Uh, Captain, don't you think
Starfleet

00:18:20.533 --> 00:18:21.447
would frown on that?

00:18:21.491 --> 00:18:23.188
We're helping a traveler
in need.

00:18:23.232 --> 00:18:26.017
We'll just tell them we lost
the shuttle in a black hole.

00:18:26.060 --> 00:18:27.236
Wouldn't be the first.

00:18:27.279 --> 00:18:29.325
Oh, I had so many personal items

00:18:29.368 --> 00:18:30.848
aboard the &lt;i&gt;Ladyjane&lt;/i&gt; too,

00:18:30.891 --> 00:18:32.328
that could never be replaced.

00:18:32.371 --> 00:18:34.068
We're talking rare antiques.

00:18:34.112 --> 00:18:36.810
-Like what?
-Oh, an old model sailing ship,

00:18:36.854 --> 00:18:41.293
a nautilus shell, bronze
pineapple, little Gorn doll.

00:18:41.337 --> 00:18:43.600
These hold special meaning
to me.

00:18:43.643 --> 00:18:46.559
Well, I guess we have
similar taste.

00:18:58.615 --> 00:19:00.791
I wish Mariner was
a super soldier.

00:19:00.834 --> 00:19:02.662
Or if only we had
special powers.

00:19:02.706 --> 00:19:06.362
Wait, we do. I mean,
maybe not here, but here.

00:19:06.405 --> 00:19:07.754
-Our skin!
-Our brains.

00:19:07.798 --> 00:19:08.929
-Brains, right.
-It's our brains.

00:19:08.973 --> 00:19:10.540
Brains are inside of our skins.

00:19:18.809 --> 00:19:22.247
I treat over 100
different species on this ship.

00:19:22.291 --> 00:19:24.249
I think I'd know if I'm healthy.

00:19:24.293 --> 00:19:26.338
Then just let me scan you!

00:19:26.382 --> 00:19:28.427
I don't need a second opinion.

00:19:30.124 --> 00:19:32.736
My arm!

00:19:32.779 --> 00:19:33.998
It's broken!

00:19:34.041 --> 00:19:35.913
Oh, nice, the old
"fake an injury" thing?

00:19:35.956 --> 00:19:38.263
Yeah, I'm not gonna fall for--
Oh, [bleep]!

00:19:38.307 --> 00:19:41.266
God, kid, I'm sorry.
This is all my...

00:19:42.572 --> 00:19:45.575
Got ya.

00:19:45.618 --> 00:19:48.839
Well played.
That was actually kinda quick.

00:19:48.882 --> 00:19:51.015
I don't know why I made
such a big thing of it.

00:19:51.058 --> 00:19:53.365
You know you guys can just
replicate stuff, right?

00:19:53.409 --> 00:19:55.454
Like the-the stuff you buy
with latinum,

00:19:55.498 --> 00:19:57.369
you could just replicate.
You guys are dumb.

00:19:57.413 --> 00:20:01.547
If we're so dumb, then how did
we capture you, human?

00:20:01.591 --> 00:20:03.245
You guys are what,
some creepy throwback

00:20:03.288 --> 00:20:05.551
&lt;i&gt;Last Outpost&lt;/i&gt; style Ferengi?
You ever heard of Quark?

00:20:05.595 --> 00:20:07.161
Of course I've heard of Quark!

00:20:07.205 --> 00:20:09.773
-♪

00:20:09.816 --> 00:20:11.296
Starfleet!

00:20:11.340 --> 00:20:14.430
Hey, Ferengi! We've got
a little somethin' for ya!

00:20:14.473 --> 00:20:17.520
May we present...

00:20:17.563 --> 00:20:21.001
a cost/benefit analysis
for greater long-term profits.

00:20:21.045 --> 00:20:25.179
What if I told you
you could earn 150% more latinum

00:20:25.223 --> 00:20:27.921
with live mugatos
rather than dead ones?

00:20:27.965 --> 00:20:31.185
Stay your whip.
What do you propose?

00:20:31.229 --> 00:20:32.491
Well...

00:20:32.535 --> 00:20:34.450
By ending the sale
or slaughter of the mugato

00:20:34.493 --> 00:20:36.365
while putting an investment
in the conversion

00:20:36.408 --> 00:20:38.584
of this place into more
of a mugato preserve...

00:20:38.628 --> 00:20:41.370
Your long-term revenue streams
will come to include

00:20:41.413 --> 00:20:45.896
ticket prices, merchandise,
concessions-- the whole gumato!

00:20:48.681 --> 00:20:50.509
Oh, Mariner,
wh-what's happening?

00:20:50.553 --> 00:20:53.643
Those two beautiful, nerdy men
are negotiating us to safety

00:20:53.686 --> 00:20:56.515
using the power of math.

00:20:57.864 --> 00:20:59.779
It is a more
time-consuming effort

00:20:59.823 --> 00:21:01.215
than our current operation,

00:21:01.259 --> 00:21:04.044
but I can't argue
with the profit margin.

00:21:04.088 --> 00:21:06.743
Though I don't love
releasing captives.

00:21:06.786 --> 00:21:09.528
Well, technically we really
should be apprehending you

00:21:09.572 --> 00:21:11.530
for attacking members
of Starfleet, so...

00:21:11.574 --> 00:21:14.316
If we're both unhappy,
that means we've reached...

00:21:14.359 --> 00:21:16.970
A compromise!
-Compromise.

00:21:20.104 --> 00:21:22.193
Mugutu venom can have
latent effects,

00:21:22.236 --> 00:21:23.673
so I'll need to check
on you later.

00:21:23.716 --> 00:21:26.240
In your quarters.

00:21:26.284 --> 00:21:31.245
I just got my physical.
I could heal you all night.

00:21:34.292 --> 00:21:37.208
Okay, people! It's go time!

00:21:37.251 --> 00:21:40.777
No, I've got this! Gimme 20cc's
of space, all right?!

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:42.213
Now that's confidence.

00:21:42.256 --> 00:21:44.128
You really showed me something
today, kid.

00:21:44.171 --> 00:21:46.304
-Thank you, Doctor.
-But this isn't your patient,

00:21:46.348 --> 00:21:47.479
so get the
out of our way.

00:21:47.523 --> 00:21:48.915
Yes, Doctor.

00:21:49.960 --> 00:21:51.918
Leaving the Frylon system now.

00:21:51.962 --> 00:21:54.268
Oh, you're gonna love this.

00:21:54.312 --> 00:21:56.140
We made contact with a group of

00:21:56.183 --> 00:21:58.534
-eco-friendly Ferengi. &lt;i&gt;
-Really?&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:58.577 --> 00:22:01.580
Apparently they're looking
to nurture abandoned mugato.

00:22:01.624 --> 00:22:04.496
Setting up a whole preserve.
Very noble.

00:22:04.540 --> 00:22:06.585
&lt;i&gt;That's outstanding.
Oh, before you go,&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:06.629 --> 00:22:08.935
&lt;i&gt;you haven't had any
recent ship accidents, have you?&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:08.979 --> 00:22:12.417
-Uh, no, nothing here. &lt;i&gt;
-Okay, good.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:12.461 --> 00:22:15.115
&lt;i&gt;We've had some reports of a scam
being run in that sector.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:15.159 --> 00:22:17.640
&lt;i&gt;Junk ship will purposefully
self-destruct&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:17.683 --> 00:22:19.032
&lt;i&gt;and try to pin it on Starfleet.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:19.076 --> 00:22:21.383
We'll be sure
to look out for that.

00:22:21.426 --> 00:22:24.603
&lt;i&gt;Did you redecorate?
Something looks different.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:28.477 --> 00:22:30.653
Way I see it, you can either
pay for your crimes

00:22:30.696 --> 00:22:32.655
in a Federation penal colony,

00:22:32.698 --> 00:22:36.267
or we can pretend you never
pulled this little stunt,

00:22:36.310 --> 00:22:38.748
and you can do some good
for a change.

00:22:38.791 --> 00:22:41.490
What do you mean, "good"?

00:22:44.318 --> 00:22:46.146
We need to get all this dung
out of here

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:47.844
so we can set up a gift shop.

00:22:47.887 --> 00:22:49.628
We're going to be rich.

00:22:49.672 --> 00:22:51.891
-From now on,

00:22:51.935 --> 00:22:53.980
we work for the mugatos.

00:22:54.024 --> 00:22:56.548
This place has to be
a horned heaven!

00:22:58.376 --> 00:23:01.248
No, you only reveal
the graph at the end.

00:23:01.292 --> 00:23:03.207
Well, can you inflate
the numbers?

00:23:03.250 --> 00:23:04.861
Wait, are you being serious?

00:23:04.904 --> 00:23:06.166
I guess not.

00:23:06.210 --> 00:23:08.081
Sorry we thought you were
a secret super spy

00:23:08.125 --> 00:23:09.692
who was ready
to kill us, by the way.

00:23:09.735 --> 00:23:11.345
In retrospect, it probably
would have come up before.

00:23:11.389 --> 00:23:13.347
And I'm sorry I spread a rumor

00:23:13.391 --> 00:23:15.219
and made you feel like you
weren't my equals,

00:23:15.262 --> 00:23:17.177
because today
you were the badasses.

00:23:17.221 --> 00:23:18.657
I guess I kick ass one way,

00:23:18.701 --> 00:23:20.877
-and you guys do it another.
-Thanks, Mariner.

00:23:20.920 --> 00:23:22.748
So what is happening
in this game?

00:23:22.792 --> 00:23:23.880
Are we almost at a compromise?

00:23:23.923 --> 00:23:25.229
No, not even close.

00:23:25.272 --> 00:23:27.013
Do you even understand
how to play this at all?

00:23:27.057 --> 00:23:28.754
I-I guess I don't.

00:23:28.798 --> 00:23:30.277
I'm gonna go grab another round.

00:23:30.321 --> 00:23:32.541
How is she kicking
our asses so hard?

00:23:32.584 --> 00:23:34.673
I don't know, but we gotta
make sure she never finds out.

00:23:34.717 --> 00:23:38.024
-What can I get you, Mariner?
-Three of the same.

00:23:38.068 --> 00:23:40.026
Hey. You see those
two guys back there?

00:23:40.070 --> 00:23:42.028
Those are the Mugato Twins.

00:23:42.072 --> 00:23:44.291
Fought off a dozen mugatos
barehanded.

00:23:44.335 --> 00:23:46.119
Then they ground up
their mugato horns,

00:23:46.163 --> 00:23:48.557
snorted 'em,
and acquired strange powers.

00:23:48.600 --> 00:23:51.560
Whoa. Well,
your secret's safe with me.

00:23:51.603 --> 00:23:53.257
Honus! Are you kidding me?

00:23:53.300 --> 00:23:55.694
I needed those limes yesterday!

00:23:55.738 --> 00:23:58.088
For real, man, if you don't
want to work at the bar,

00:23:58.131 --> 00:24:00.133
don't work at the bar.

00:25:03.501 --> 00:25:03.762
Chirp.
